From 788bc438a07178b1233d34c658d7a98d38e2746d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:49:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Credit-vault submitter role: opt-in local verifier state and
 validated receipt source

The hosted credit-vault submitter (network/credit-vault-submitter.mjs, role
network/host-services/credit-vault-submitter.mjs) hardcoded a provider
QuorumChain and RPC reader. It now builds both through the CLI's own creation
path (cli/credit-vault.mjs readerFor/chainFor, chainFor now exported) and
accepts two state authorities:

- provider quorum (unchanged, compatible): rpc = 2-8 providers that must agree;
  /health and the log now say so plainly ("agreement between providers, not
  proof");
- chainVerifier (opt-in): the operator's local proof-backed verifier answers
  every state read and simulation; rpc is then only the explicit transaction
  transport (1-8 endpoints, e.g. the operator's own node), never state, so no
  public provider list is required. Optional receiptSource: the inline
  enclave-receipt-source/v1 config of the local L1 pair + Base node, parsed and
  built (no I/O; E's adapters enforce loopback) at the runner's intake by the
  same glue as the CLI (network/receipt-source.mjs). Its test-fixture identities
  are refused unless ENCLAVE_TEST_RECEIPT_FIXTURE=1 is in the validating
  process's environment; the host-service runner passes none to the role.
  outcomeTimeoutSec (10-600, default 180) bounds how long a send waits before it
  is held as unknown.

The relay keeps exact bytes, one flight per digest, the operator's external
signer (its journal now settles on minted receipts bound to the signed bytes
when a receipt source is set), and unknown outcomes held, never re-signed. Its
success answer adds the verified outcome text under the verifier; /health adds
`authority` (state, transactions, receipts) via cli/credit-vault.mjs
relayAuthority, also used by `enclave credit-vault relay`.

Tests: test/credit-vault-submitter-config.test.mjs (intake, labels, runner
validator) and test/credit-vault-submitter-verifier.e2e.test.mjs (the PACKAGED
role on reth --dev + Helios + anvil L1 + E's labelled beacon/rollup fixtures:
exact success, idempotent bytes, a real on-chain revert, tampered proofs, admin
book migration, unknown held and recovered by rebroadcasting the same bytes,
and through the runner: no environment, a not-ready production source ending
unknown, the platform host policy gate).
